 "notes": "All three photos are single pages rotated 90 deg (top of text at the left); read after rotating 90 deg clockwise. No bifolium; only L-lines.\nGLYPH DECISIONS: the frequent lone glyph like a 4/phi (open cup with a vertical stem through it, z. ex. 702 L6 '25.psi.1', 703 L10 '25.psi.16') is transcribed SYM:psi throughout (it is distinct from the digit 4 inside 34/44/94). SYM:q-barré = a '9' whose stem carries a horizontal bar (sometimes with a dot under it): 702 L14 before final 96, 703 L9, 705 L5. SYM:pi = small low 'pi'. Strokes read as '3' with a tail before a '1' (31) could be 51 with a long-s 5; I chose 31 by comparison with 33. 703 L10 '91' has a closed bowl (could be 31 too), with two dots over it that may be a stain.\nP1370702: L6 '26': a stroke in the darker annotation ink crosses the 2 (not counted as a mark). L7 last token 99 carries a vertical stroke flanked by dots (marked other?). L19: 'SYM:autre-II-barré-haut-et-bas' = two vertical strokes between a top and a bottom bar (like roman II / Pi with foot bar); 'SYM:autre-y' = y-shaped sign. L18: after 'Dites a 97' a word in clear was crossed out (heavy blot) and the run 21.83.67.69.55 is written above it in the original ink (placed there as an interlinear replacement run). L20 clear line ends with a light struck/illegible stretch. LATER ANNOTATIONS in darker brown ink (not tokens): above L6 cipher 'n'y avoir aucun esgard'?; above 82.74 (L8) 'mr le'; above L9 cipher 'presydent d'apres'?; above L10 cipher 'du retour des deputés'; above L11 cipher 'laisser mr ... [?]'; above L21 cipher 'tadessus'? (crossed); left margin beside L18-L21: 'qu'il tienne tous les choses en bon estat encore pour quelque temps'. Archive stamp (Dordogne) over left of L13-L15; shelfmark '2E 1841/18 - 11' in blue at bottom; '1651' pencil top left.\nP1370703: final page of a letter (closing + signature 'Louis de Bourbon', dated 'De Paris le 25 Aoust 1651') then a postscript with cipher dated 'ce 27e Aoust' and signed again. Faint brown offsets (mirror-image transfer from annotations of a facing page) near 'Monsieur' and left of 'Depuis'; not transcribed. L15: the last tokens (27, 46, 66) are overlapped by later brown-ink annotation (offset/annotation 'qu'il tienne fay...' bleeding at right margin), so 27 and the mark on 66 are uncertain; 24 could be 2+psi? read as 24. L12 '65' bar looks straight (macron?). Docket at bottom left 'M. Du[Chambon?]' (reading uncertain).\nP1370705: header '1651. 13. Aoust.' (later hand?). L5: a word after 'avoit faict' struck out with '49' written above it (taken as the replacement). L6: over the psi before SYM:m there is a small m-like wavy squiggle (possibly a superscript m or a tilde on the symbol) - not encoded. L11/L14: 'SYM:autre-x-souligné' = x with a curved stroke underneath (distinct from the plain x in L5). L12 '19|other' = two short vertical strokes (double acute) above. L18 '75': the mark is a long stroke running from 75 toward 19 (tilde?). L23: a thin vertical line between 67 and 69 is a stray stroke/crease, not a token. Clear 'Bdx' (Bordeaux) in L17 has an abbreviation mark. Archive stamp left of L18-L20; shelfmark '2E 1841/18 - 12'."
